  SOURCE               INTERMEDIATE (lazy)           TERMINAL (triggers all)
  ──────               ─────────────────────         ──────────────────────
  Collection.stream()  .filter(Predicate)            .collect(Collector)
  Arrays.stream()      .map(Function)                .toList()
  Stream.of()          .flatMap(Function)            .forEach(Consumer)
  Stream.generate()    .sorted(Comparator)           .reduce(identity, BinaryOp)
  Files.lines()        .distinct()                   .count()
  Stream.iterate()     .limit(n)  .skip(n)          .findFirst() / .findAny()
                       .peek(Consumer)               .anyMatch/allMatch/noneMatch

  ═══ IMPERATIVE vs STREAM — SAME LOGIC ═══

  IMPERATIVE (5 loops, 40 lines):
    List<Trade> settled = new ArrayList<>();
    for (Trade t : all) { if (t.isSettled()) settled.add(t); }
    BigDecimal totalBuy = ZERO;
    for (Trade t : settled) { if (t.isBuy()) totalBuy = totalBuy.add(t.getAmount()); }
    BigDecimal totalSell = ZERO;
    for (Trade t : settled) { if (!t.isBuy()) totalSell = totalSell.add(t.getAmount()); }
    Set<String> symbols = new TreeSet<>();
    for (Trade t : settled) { symbols.add(t.getSymbol()); }

  STREAM (4 pipelines, 12 lines):
    settled = all.stream().filter(Trade::isSettled).toList();
    totalBuy = settled.stream().filter(Trade::isBuy).map(Trade::getAmount).reduce(ZERO, add);
    totalSell = settled.stream().filter(t -> !t.isBuy()).map(Trade::getAmount).reduce(ZERO, add);
    symbols = settled.stream().map(Trade::getSymbol).distinct().sorted().toList();

  ═══ 5 KEY DIFFERENCES ═══

  Collection                      │  Stream
  ────────────────────────────────│──────────────────────────────
  STORES elements (ArrayList)     │  Stores NOTHING (pipeline)
  EAGER — all computed upfront    │  LAZY — computed on terminal
  REUSABLE — iterate many times   │  SINGLE-USE — consumed once
  IMPERATIVE — for/if/accumulator │  DECLARATIVE — filter/map/reduce
  Manual parallelism              │  .parallelStream() built-in

  ═══ SINGLE-USE PROOF ═══

  Stream<String> s = list.stream().filter(...);
  s.count();        // (Recommended) OK — terminal consumes stream
  s.forEach(...);   // (Avoid) IllegalStateException! Already consumed!
  // Fix: create new stream — list.stream().filter(...)...
